Terminal commands to reduce the files size and strip attributes from the original EEZ_land_union_v4_202410.geojson file

for this to work, we need to install ogr2ogr, which is a part of GDAL:
brew install gdal

1. step: convert the shapefile to GeoJSON

ogr2ogr \
  -f GeoJSON \
  EEZ_land_union_v4_202410.geojson \
  EEZ_land_union_v4_202410.shp

  
2. step: simplify the polygon geometry,  keeping it as accurate as possible while getting the file size down (resolution 0.001° ≈ 110 m latitude)

ogr2ogr \
  -f GeoJSON \
  EEZ_land_union_v4_202410_simplified_0p001.geojson \
  EEZ_land_union_v4_202410.geojson \
  -simplify 0.001

  
3. step: retain only the SOVEREIGN1 and TERRITORY1 fields 
  
ogr2ogr \
  -f GeoJSON \
  EEZ_land_union_v4_202410_minimal_0p001_sov_terr.geojson \
  EEZ_land_union_v4_202410_simplified_0p001.geojson \
  -select SOVEREIGN1,TERRITORY1
